### CRM calendar API (spec §6.2, A29) — staff only
# Works with the REST Client (VS Code) / JetBrains HTTP Client.
# 1. `docker compose up mongo`, `pnpm seed`, `pnpm dev`.
# 2. Run "login" (admin / manager / barber1 of the seed, password = SEED_PASSWORD) and put the `token`
#    into @token. The admin cookie works too (same origin).
# 3. Run "calendar", copy ids into the variables below.
#
# Auth: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; no user → 401 UNAUTHORIZED, editor → 403 FORBIDDEN.
# Errors: `{ "error": { "code": "SLOT_TAKEN", "details": { ... } } }`, the HTTP status matches the type.
# Codes: UNAUTHORIZED, FORBIDDEN, NOT_FOUND (also for appointments outside the user's scope),
# VALIDATION_ERROR (details.fields), LOCATION_NOT_FOUND, BARBER_NOT_FOUND, PHONE_INVALID,
# CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED (409, details.warnings [+ details.total {from, to}]) and the service codes:
# SLOT_TAKEN, SLOT_UNAVAILABLE, BARBER_LOCATION_INVALID, BLOCK_TIME_INVALID, SERVICE_REQUIRED,
# SERVICE_NOT_FOUND, EXTRA_NOT_FOUND, EXTRA_NOT_APPLICABLE, APPOINTMENT_FORBIDDEN, APPOINTMENT_PAID_LOCKED,
# DISCOUNT_FORBIDDEN, DISCOUNT_INVALID, DISCOUNT_TOO_LARGE, DISCOUNT_REASON_REQUIRED, PROMO_*,
# STATUS_TRANSITION_INVALID, STATUS_TOO_EARLY, STATUS_FORBIDDEN, CANCEL_REASON_REQUIRED.
# Warnings to confirm (repeat the same request with "confirm": true):
# OUTSIDE_SCHEDULE, PRICE_CHANGED, HAS_PAYMENTS, REFUND_REQUIRED.
# Money — integer bani (MDL × 100); instants — ISO UTC; dates — local `YYYY-MM-DD` (Europe/Chisinau).

@api = http://localhost:3000/api
@token = paste-the-login-token
@location = 000000000000000000000000
@barber = 000000000000000000000000
@barber2 = 000000000000000000000000
@service = 000000000000000000000000
@extra = 000000000000000000000000
@client = 000000000000000000000000
@appointment = 000000000000000000000000
@date = 2026-12-14

### Login (standard Payload auth) → `token`
POST {{api}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@levelup.local", "password": "levelup-dev-123" }

### Calendar, day: columns = barbers of the location (own column first for a barber),
### working intervals in the location (`off`: no_schedule | day_off | vacation | sick | other_location),
### appointments — full details, or `{ start, end, busy }` for rows the user may not read.
### `location` defaults to the first visible one; `cancelled=1` adds cancelled appointments.
GET {{api}}/crm/calendar?date={{date}}&view=day&location={{location}}&locale=ru
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Calendar, week (A2): 7 columns (Mon…Sun) of one barber (a barber — their own by default)
GET {{api}}/crm/calendar?date={{date}}&view=week&location={{location}}&barber={{barber}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Staff slots (§5.3 p.7): every grid step without an overlap; outside the schedule → OUTSIDE_SCHEDULE.
### `barber` empty/any = every barber of the location (admin, manager); a barber gets only their own.
### Editing: `exclude` = the appointment (its time is free), `duration` = its snapshot duration.
GET {{api}}/crm/slots?location={{location}}&barber={{barber}}&service={{service}}&extras[]={{extra}}&date={{date}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Client by phone (admin, manager) → { client: {...} | null }
GET {{api}}/crm/clients/lookup?phone=069100001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an appointment (client: null = "without a name"; a barber may omit `barber` — their own)
POST {{api}}/crm/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": "{{location}}",
  "barber": "{{barber}}",
  "client": "{{client}}",
  "service": "{{service}}",
  "extras": ["{{extra}}"],
  "start": "2026-12-14T08:00:00.000Z",
  "promoCode": "LEVELUP10",
  "manualDiscount": { "type": "percent", "value": 10, "reason": "Regular client" },
  "clientComment": null,
  "internalNote": "Prefers scissors",
  "language": "ro"
}

### Same time outside the schedule → 409 CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED { warnings: ["OUTSIDE_SCHEDULE"] };
### repeat with "confirm": true
POST {{api}}/crm/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": "{{location}}",
  "barber": "{{barber}}",
  "client": null,
  "service": "{{service}}",
  "start": "2026-12-14T18:00:00.000Z",
  "confirm": true
}

### Time block (decision 21): no client/service, own duration
POST {{api}}/crm/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "block",
  "location": "{{location}}",
  "barber": "{{barber}}",
  "start": "2026-12-14T11:00:00.000Z",
  "durationMinutes": 60
}

### Move to another barber/time (drag-n-drop): price recalculated → 409 PRICE_CHANGED
### { total: { from, to } } (+ HAS_PAYMENTS if paid); repeat with "confirm": true. Queues the "moved" email.
PATCH {{api}}/crm/appointments/{{appointment}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "barber": "{{barber2}}",
  "start": "2026-12-14T09:00:00.000Z"
}

### Change composition, promo code (null removes it), discount (null removes it), notes
PATCH {{api}}/crm/appointments/{{appointment}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "service": "{{service}}",
  "extras": [],
  "promoCode": null,
  "manualDiscount": { "type": "amount", "value": 5000, "reason": "Waited" },
  "internalNote": "Late 10 min"
}

### Status (§5.1): completed | no_show | cancelled_by_client | cancelled_by_salon (reason) | scheduled (restore)
### Cancelling an appointment with payments → 409 REFUND_REQUIRED; repeat with "confirm": true
POST {{api}}/crm/appointments/{{appointment}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "cancelled_by_salon", "reason": "Barber is ill" }

### Modal data (stage 15): details, price lines with names, promo code text, change history (newest first)
### and what the role may do. A barber gets their own appointments only (404 otherwise); user e-mails in
### the history — admin/manager only.
GET {{api}}/crm/appointments/{{appointment}}?locale=ru
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Price preview (no write): the same pricing as on save. Barber: own column, no manualDiscount (403).
POST {{api}}/crm/appointments/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": "{{location}}",
  "barber": "{{barber}}",
  "service": "{{service}}",
  "extras": ["{{extra}}"],
  "promoCode": "LEVELUP10",
  "manualDiscount": { "type": "percent", "value": 10, "reason": "Regular client" }
}

### A client typed as phone (+ name): the server links the card of that phone or creates one (source "staff").
### Works for every role (a barber has no lookup). An explicit "client" id wins; also accepted by PATCH.
POST {{api}}/crm/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": "{{location}}",
  "barber": "{{barber}}",
  "service": "{{service}}",
  "start": "2026-12-14T08:00:00.000Z",
  "clientPhone": "069 123 456",
  "clientFirstName": "Vlad",
  "clientLastName": "Popa"
}

### Ledger (stage 17). Expenses, transfers and adjustments go through the standard REST collection
### `/api/transactions` (the hook checks the type rules, registers, role, day; balances change by `$inc`).
POST {{api}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "expense",
  "location": "{{location}}",
  "expenseCategory": "{{expenseCategory}}",
  "entries": [{ "cashRegister": "{{cashRegister}}", "amount": -45000 }],
  "comment": "Shampoo"
}

### Reversal: the mirror operation; the original gets `reversed = true` (once).
### Manager: own locations, operations of the current day (expense/transfer); out of scope → 404.
### → { transaction, original, warnings: ["NEGATIVE_BALANCE"]? }
POST {{api}}/crm/transactions/{{transaction}}/reverse
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "comment": "Wrong amount" }

### Certificate sale (stage 18): the certificate (code LU-XXXX-XXXX, balance = nominal, valid 12 months
### by default) + `certificate_sale` in one transaction. Admin; manager — registers of own locations.
### → { certificate, transaction, warnings }
POST {{api}}/crm/certificates/sell
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nominal": 50000,
  "entries": [{ "cashRegister": "{{cashRegister}}", "amount": 50000 }],
  "buyer": { "name": "Maria", "phone": "069 123 456" },
  "comment": "Birthday"
}

### Appointment payment: registers of the appointment's location, optional certificate (by default it
### covers what the money does not), tip (from the money only). Overpayment → 409 PAYMENT_EXCEEDS_DUE.
### Barber — own appointments; manager — own locations; out of scope → 404.
### → { transaction, appointment, certificate: { id, code, balance } | null, warnings }
POST {{api}}/crm/appointments/{{appointment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entries": [
    { "cashRegister": "{{cashRegister}}", "amount": 10000 },
    { "cashRegister": "{{cardRegister}}", "amount": 15000 }
  ],
  "tip": 5000,
  "certificateCode": "LU-ABCD-EFGH",
  "certificateAmount": 10000
}

### Refund of a payment (admin): mirror entries, the certificate part goes back to the certificate,
### `paid → completed`, `paymentStatus = refunded` when nothing is left paid. Second refund → 409.
### → { transaction, original, appointment, certificate: { id, balance } | null, warnings }
POST {{api}}/crm/transactions/{{payment}}/refund
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "comment": "Client unhappy" }

### Schedule exception preview (stage 20): scheduled appointments of the barber in the date range,
### shown as a warning before a day off / vacation / custom hours is created from the calendar.
### → { count, appointments: [{ id, start }] }; admin and the manager of the barber, otherwise 403
GET {{api}}/crm/schedule-exceptions/preview?barber={{barber}}&dateFrom=2026-12-14&dateTo=2026-12-20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
